# LIKELY JUDGE QUESTIONS
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. What does Nemotron actually do here, and what happens if it's slow or
#    down?
#    Nemotron explains every block in plain language for the reviewer, and its
#    checks can escalate a call to a human. A live call adds about 0.7 seconds
#    at the median, and if the API rate-limits us, Leash falls back to local
#    detectors. Since Nemotron can only add caution, a failure never unblocks
#    anything.
#
# 2. What does Leash miss?
#    Our Nemotron evaluation is small, just 40 labelled cases, and in the final
#    holdout run two of the three injected documents got past every detector.
#    The live agent also isn't deterministic: it followed the hidden
#    instruction in only 1 of 3 unprotected runs. That's why the scripted
#    replay is our demo of record, and a bigger labelled set is the first thing
#    we'd add.
#
# 3. Is this HIPAA compliant? Could a hospital use it tomorrow?
#    No. It's a prototype on synthetic data with one role and one policy. We
#    mapped our controls to HIPAA rules in docs/HIPAA_MAPPING.md as a design
